From 3d93419448acc206b9ecb1ca86eb32718f7ba8c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:14:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 60/61] LOCAL DEBUG: pvr: PVR_MEM_REPORT=<seconds> prints the
 device's live GPU memory

Debug aid for amazon-sheldonp's memory accounting; never sent. fdinfo
gives one number per DRM file, and PVR_LOG_ALLOC logs allocations but no
frees, so neither says what a process holds right now. With
PVR_MEM_REPORT=N each device counts its live vkAllocateMemory (own and
imported) and its own pvr_bo_alloc buffers by heap, and prints one line
to stderr at most every N seconds from queue submission and at device
destruction, with the SPM scratch buffer the store holds. Off by default
(no counting).

Generated-by: LLM
